## Summary
`openclaw doctor --fix` widens `skills.allowBundled` to allow every bundled skill when `nano-banana-pro` is the only entry in it. The retired-skill migration filters `nano-banana-pro` out of the list and, when nothing is left, deletes the key. An absent `skills.allowBundled` means "no bundled allowlist" (every bundled skill is eligible), while an empty list means "no bundled skills" (`docs/tools/skills-config.md`: "an empty list disables all bundled skills", made explicit by #182731). An operator who had restricted bundled skills to that single skill ends up with all of them loaded after a routine `doctor --fix`.

## Root cause
`normalizeLegacyNanoBananaSkill` in `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-core-normalizers.ts` special-cases the empty result:

```ts
// before
if (filtered.length !== skills.allowBundled.length) {
  if (filtered.length) {
    skills.allowBundled = filtered;
    changes.push(`Removed ${key} from skills.allowBundled.`);
  } else {
    delete skills.allowBundled;
    changes.push(`Removed skills.allowBundled entry for ${key}.`);
  }
}
```

The runtime reads the allowlist in `resolveBundledAllowlist` (`src/skills/loading/config.ts`): `undefined` returns no allowlist, so `isBundledSkillAllowed` admits every bundled skill; `[]` returns an empty set, so none are admitted. Deleting the key flips the meaning from deny-all-but-one to allow-all.

## Fix
Keep the filtered list in both cases, so removing the retired entry never changes which other bundled skills are eligible:

```ts
// after
if (filtered.length !== skills.allowBundled.length) {
  skills.allowBundled = filtered;
  changes.push(`Removed ${key} from skills.allowBundled.`);
}
```

## Why this is the right boundary
The migration is the only writer that removes entries from `skills.allowBundled` (no other Doctor or config path touches the key), and the runtime contract for an empty list is already settled and documented, so the fix belongs at the migration rather than in the skills loader. Lists that still hold other skills are filtered exactly as before, configs without `nano-banana-pro` are untouched, and the `skills.entries.nano-banana-pro` image-model migration below it is unchanged. The production diff only deletes the branch that dropped the key.

## Verification
- `src/commands/doctor-legacy-config.migrations.test.ts`: the existing `skills.allowBundled` migration case now uses `["nano-banana-pro"]` and asserts the migrated config keeps `allowBundled: []` with the change note `Removed nano-banana-pro from skills.allowBundled.`. It fails on main (the key is deleted) and passes with the patch; the rest of the file (26 cases) passes.
- `oxfmt --check` is clean on both changed files.
- Local tsgo and oxlint were not run per the contributor workflow for this batch; GitHub Actions covers them.

