## Summary
A Gemini model configured with nucleus sampling (`agents.defaults.models["google/<model>"].params.topP`, or the documented `params.top_p` alias) sends no `topP` to Google. The shared extra-params wrapper resolves either spelling into the `topP` stream option, as `docs/gateway/config-agents/models.md` documents ("Nucleus sampling accepts `params.topP` or `params.top_p`"), and OpenAI and Ollama honor it, but every Google request builder drops it. `temperature` from the same `params` block does reach the request, so the dropped value is silent.

## Root cause
The Google transports copy only `temperature`, `maxTokens` and `stop` from the stream options into the request. `extensions/google/transport-stream.ts` (`buildGoogleGenerativeAiParams`, used for Gemini API and Vertex turns):

```ts
// before
if (typeof options?.temperature === "number") {
  generationConfig.temperature = options.temperature;
}
if (options?.stop !== undefined && options.stop.length > 0) {
  generationConfig.stopSequences = options.stop;
}
```

The same gap exists in `packages/ai/src/providers/google-interactions-request.ts` (`buildGoogleInteractionsParams`, whose request type already declares `generation_config.top_p` but never sets it) and in `packages/ai/src/providers/google-shared.ts` (`buildGoogleGenerateContentParams`, the built-in Gemini path).

## Fix
Each Google request builder maps the `topP` stream option to its native field, next to `temperature`:

```ts
// after
if (typeof options?.temperature === "number") {
  generationConfig.temperature = options.temperature;
}
if (typeof options?.topP === "number") {
  generationConfig.topP = options.topP;
}
```

Interactions writes `generation_config.top_p`, and the built-in generateContent builder writes `config.topP`. `GoogleTransportOptions` and `GoogleProviderOptions` gain `topP?: number`, matching how the OpenAI and Ollama transports type the same option.

## Why this is the right boundary
Config resolution is already correct: `createStreamFnWithExtraParams` resolves `topP`/`top_p` into one `topP` stream option for every provider, and the OpenAI and Ollama transports consume it. The drop happens only where the Google transports build their wire payload, so the mapping belongs in those builders. All three Google request shapes (generateContent via the plugin, Interactions, and the built-in generateContent path) are covered so no Google route keeps the gap. Nothing is sent unless `topP` is configured or passed per request, so existing requests are byte-identical. Other transports are untouched.

## Verification
- `extensions/google/transport-stream.request-config.test.ts`: the generation config built by `buildGoogleGenerativeAiParams` now includes `topP: 0.4` next to temperature, max output tokens and stop sequences.
- `packages/ai/src/providers/google-interactions-shared.convert.test.ts`: `buildGoogleInteractionsParams` emits `generation_config: { temperature: 0.2, top_p: 0.4 }`.
- `packages/ai/src/providers/google-shared.test.ts`: `buildGoogleGenerateContentParams` emits `config.topP`.
- Each of the three files was run with `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs <file>`: the new assertions fail on pristine main and pass with the patch. `oxfmt --check` is clean on all changed files.
- Local tsgo and oxlint were not run per the contributor workflow for this batch; GitHub Actions covers them.

