Related: #185225

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: a shared session stays out of Involving me when a webchat author sends a message that is stored, then skipped or recovered before reply initialization.

## User Impact

User impact: once a person's webchat message is accepted into a session, that person is a session participant, so Involving me can include the session even if the turn never finishes reply init.

## Why This Change Was Made

chat.send prepared the author on the in-memory turn. The durable participant row was written later, and only when reply init ran for a normal turn. Restart recovery answers as an internal system turn, and a follow-up skipped because another reply is active returns before that write.

The accept path now records the prepared author when the visible human message is staged, and when that original message is appended. The existing recorded flag keeps the contribution at one if reply init later records the same turn. Internal, hidden, and excluded messages are not recorded.

A dashboard webchat conversation bound to an ACP session is recorded on that ACP session. The dashboard session does not receive the author, and the fact is consumed only after the write lands. If the binding lookup fails, the accept path does not record anyone and does not consume the fact, so ACP admission can still record the author on the bound session.

A staged message that is later cancelled still leaves the author on the session, because that stage already accepted the input. This pull does not change which runs main-session restart recovery adopts. That part of #185225 is separate.

